---
title: Project log
layout: home
description: What shipped, in order — a stepper of dated entries with the version, what changed, and a shot of it. The project's history as a page of its own, not a section at the bottom of one.
eyebrow: Collections · Project
source: src/components/repo-card.css · timeline.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Project · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 2rem">
		<header class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .75rem">
			<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
				<ol class="im-breadcrumb im-breadcrumb-chevron">
					<li><a href="/">{{> "icons/house"}}<span>Home</span></a></li>
					<li><a href="/collections/project/">{{> "icons/folder"}}<span>Projects</span></a></li>
					<li><a href="/collections/project/page/">im-design-system</a></li>
					<li><span aria-current="page">Log</span></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>
			<p><span class="im-kind" data-kind="project">{{icon "git-commit-vertical"}}Log</span></p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">What shipped, and when</h1>
			<p class="im-collhead-text">Every version of <a href="/collections/project/page/">im-design-system</a> since the first one, in order, with what changed and why. It is the honest version of a changelog — the ones that got reverted are here too.</p>
			<p class="im-collhead-meta"><span>{{demo.log.length}} entries</span><span>v0.1 — v0.7</span><a href="#log">RSS</a></p>
		</header>

		<ol class="im-timeline im-timeline-numbered im-log" id="log">
			{{#each demo.log}}
			<li class="im-timeline-item" data-state="{{state}}">
				<span class="im-timeline-marker"></span>
				<time class="im-timeline-time">{{when}}</time>
				<h2 class="im-timeline-title">{{title}}</h2>
				<p class="im-timeline-text">{{text}}</p>
				{{#if shot}}<figure class="im-log-shot"><img src="{{shot}}" alt="" loading="lazy"><figcaption>{{title}}</figcaption></figure>{{/if}}
				{{#if tag}}<p class="im-log-meta"><span class="im-badge im-badge-outline">{{tag}}</span><a class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-btn-ghost" href="/collections/project/page/">{{icon "arrow-right"}}The release</a></p>{{/if}}
			</li>
			{{/each}}
		</ol>

		<div class="im-loadmore">
			<button class="im-btn" type="button">Earlier versions</button>
			<p>4 of 11</p>
		</div>
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
			<div class="im-widgets">
				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="l-proj">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="l-proj">The project</h2>
					<div class="im-widget-products">
						<a class="im-widget-product" href="/collections/project/page/"><span class="im-widget-product-mark">{{icon "folder"}}</span><span class="im-widget-product-name">im-design-system</span><span class="im-widget-product-note">The case study</span>{{icon "arrow-up-right"}}</a>
						<a class="im-widget-product" href="#log"><span class="im-widget-product-mark">{{icon "brand-github"}}</span><span class="im-widget-product-name">Source</span><span class="im-widget-product-note">1.2k stars · MIT</span>{{icon "arrow-up-right"}}</a>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="l-vers">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="l-vers">Versions</h2>
					<ol class="im-timeline im-timeline-compact im-widget-series">
						{{#each demo.log}}
						<li class="im-timeline-item" data-state="{{state}}">
							<span class="im-timeline-marker">{{#if tag}}{{tag}}{{else}}—{{/if}}</span>
							<h3 class="im-timeline-title">{{#match state "=" "current"}}<span>{{title}}</span>{{else}}<a href="#log">{{title}}</a>{{/match}}</h3>
						</li>
						{{/each}}
					</ol>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="l-notes">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="l-notes">Working notes <a href="/collections/timeline/">All</a></h2>
					<ul class="im-widget-list">
						{{#each demo.stream.[0].items}}{{#match @index "<" 3}}<li><a href="/collections/timeline/">{{title}}<small>{{when}}</small></a></li>{{/match}}{{/each}}
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill" aria-labelledby="l-sub">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="l-sub">Releases</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-heading">One email when a version ships.</p>
					{{> "components/subscribe" id="log-email" button="Join"}}
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>Why the log is its own page</h2>
		<p>On the <a href="/collections/project/page/">project page</a> the log is a section near the bottom, four entries long, and that is right for somebody deciding whether to use the thing. It is <strong>wrong</strong> for somebody who already uses it and wants to know what changed in v0.6 — they have scrolled past a case study to get to it, and there are only ever four entries there.</p>
		<p>So the log gets a URL: every version, its own RSS feed, and a page somebody can be sent a link to. The project page keeps its four and links here.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Page</th><th>For</th><th>Shows</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><a href="/collections/project/page/">Project</a></td><td>Deciding whether to use it</td><td>The case study, and the last four entries</td></tr>
				<tr><td><a href="/collections/project/log/">Log</a></td><td>Already using it</td><td>Every version, in order, with what changed</td></tr>
				<tr><td><a href="/collections/timeline/">Timeline</a></td><td>Neither — it is the working notes</td><td>What you <em>thought</em>, including what did not ship</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>
		<p>That last row is the distinction worth holding on to. <strong>The journal is what you thought; the log is what shipped.</strong> A note about a pseudo-element inheriting is a journal entry; "v0.7 — collections" is a log entry. Cross-link them — the log's rail carries the notes that went into it — but do not merge them, because one is dated by day and the other by version, and a list sorted two ways at once is sorted neither.</p>

		<h2>It is the timeline, tuned</h2>
		<p><code>im-timeline im-timeline-numbered im-log</code> — the same stepper the project page uses, at full page width. <code>data-state</code> does the work: <code>done</code> fills the mark in ink and draws a solid line, <code>current</code> puts it in the accent, <code>upcoming</code> fades the entry and dashes the line to it.</p>
		{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
{{#get "posts" filter="tag:#log+tag:#im-design-system" order="published_at desc" limit="all"}}
	<ol class="im-timeline im-timeline-numbered im-log">
		{{#foreach posts}}
		<li class="im-timeline-item" data-state="{{@custom.state}}">
			<span class="im-timeline-marker"></span>
			<time class="im-timeline-time">{{date format="MMMM YYYY"}}</time>
			<h2 class="im-timeline-title">{{title}}</h2>
			<div class="im-timeline-text">{{content}}</div>
		</li>
		{{/foreach}}
	</ol>
{{/get}}
		{{{{/code}}}}
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Keep the reverted ones.</strong> "This shipped and came back out in v0.6" is the most useful line a changelog can contain, and the only one nobody writes.</li>
			<li><strong>A shot where it helps.</strong> <code>im-log-shot</code> — for a version whose change is visual. Most are not.</li>
			<li><strong>Newest first here</strong>, unlike a <a href="/collections/series/">series</a>: somebody reading a log wants the latest, and somebody reading a series wants episode one.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
